    "title": "Count Good Nodes in a Binary Tree",
    "category": "Trees",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given a binary tree, a node is considered good if no ancestor on the path from the root has a value greater than the node's value. Determine the total number of good nodes.",
    "input": "\u2022 The first line contains an integer N. \u2022 The second line contains the node values. \u2022 The next N lines describe the binary tree.",
    "output": "\u2022 Print the number of good nodes.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 1 \u2264 N \u2264 2 \u00d7 10^5"
